{
  "_copy": [
    "COPY. The source of truth is the worker's table:",
    "  ratatosk/apps/worker/internal/version/testdata/version-golden.json",
    "Never edit this file on its own — edit the worker's, then refresh this one verbatim:",
    "  cp ../ratatosk/apps/worker/internal/version/testdata/version-golden.json internal/version/testdata/",
    "(the two files are byte-identical apart from this _copy block). It is duplicated rather than",
    "imported because this is a separate public repository, the same reason internal/version itself",
    "is a copy: the in-cluster MCP server compares versions client-side and never ships them out."
  ],
  "_readme": [
    "SSOT for release-version semantics. Three implementations must agree on this one table:",
    "  1. apps/worker/internal/version        (Go, canonical)",
    "  2. ratatosk-mcp/internal/version       (Go, copy of the canonical + Compare)",
    "  3. apps/web/src/lib/version.ts         (TS, card ordering)",
    "Each ships a golden test that reads this file, so a change in one that is not made in the",
    "other two fails a build instead of silently mis-ordering releases.",
    "",
    "Sections:",
    "  normalize  — raw tag -> integer sort key (null = unparseable, excluded from range queries)",
    "  split_line — raw tag -> {line, rest}; line \"\" is the project's main line",
    "  compare    — {a, b} -> verdict. Go verdict is SameLine-gated: \"different_line\" means the",
    "               pair has no order at all. The web needs a TOTAL order (it sorts cards), so each",
    "               case also carries web_order, the answer compareVersionsDesc must give:",
    "               main line first, then lines by name, then key descending, then raw ascending.",
    "  known_divergence — cases where the current implementation's answer is NOT the sensible one.",
    "               Asserted anyway (drift between the three copies is what this file catches), but",
    "               fenced off so nobody reads them as endorsed answers. See _why."
  ],
  "normalize": [
